---
/**
 * Privacy policy.
 *
 * Short because the site genuinely does very little. The temptation with a page
 * like this is to copy a generic template full of clauses about marketing
 * preferences and third-party advertising partners that do not exist here.
 * A privacy policy describing processing that does not happen is worse than
 * none: it is the same failure as a citation pointing at the wrong paper.
 */
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";

const updated = "14 September 2026";
---

<Base
  title="Privacy"
  description="What this site collects, which is almost nothing, and what the host logs on its behalf."
  cites={[]}
>
  <section class="section section--open">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="masthead">
        <h1>Privacy</h1>
        <p class="masthead__meta mono">Last updated {updated}</p>
      </div>

      <div class="doc">
        <p class="lede">
          This site sets no cookies and has no accounts, forms or comments. It loads one
          third-party script, Cloudflare Web Analytics, which counts page views without
          identifying visitors.
        </p>

        <h2>Information collected</h2>
        <p>
          The site provides no means of submitting information. There is no form, login, comment
          field or upload.
        </p>
        <p>
          Page views are counted using
          <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/web-analytics/">Cloudflare Web Analytics</a>. It
          records that a page was viewed, the approximate region of the request, the browser and
          device type, and the referring site where one exists. This is the only measurement on the
          site.
        </p>
        <p>
          The analytics script sets no cookie, stores nothing in the browser, performs no device
          fingerprinting and assigns no identifier. It cannot associate visits with each other or
          with activity on other sites. No advertising network is involved.
        </p>
        <p>
          The resulting data is held by Cloudflare under their privacy terms. It is not sold,
          shared or combined with other data.
        </p>

        <h2>Host processing</h2>
        <p>
          The site is served by Cloudflare, which processes requests in order to serve them and to
          protect the service from abuse. This normally includes the IP address, the page
          requested, the time of the request and the browser user agent. This occurs at the
          infrastructure layer.
        </p>
        <p>
          Cloudflare also asks browsers to report failed requests, which allows a host to detect
          outages. Successful page views are not reported by this mechanism, and these reports are
          not visible to this site.
        </p>
        <p>
          Cloudflare's retention periods are governed by
          <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">Cloudflare's privacy policy</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>Browser storage</h2>
        <p>
          This site writes no cookies, no local storage and no other client-side state. Browsers
          cache pages and fonts according to their own settings.
        </p>

        <h2>Assets</h2>
        <p>
          Fonts are served from this domain. The site carries no images, embedded video, social
          widgets or tag managers. Apart from the analytics script named above, all resources are
          served from this domain, and the content security policy blocks scripts from any other
          origin.
        </p>

        <h2>External links</h2>
        <p>
          The site links extensively to third-party pages, which are subject to their own privacy
          practices. Links to sources carry no tracking parameters.
        </p>

        <h2>Data about third parties</h2>
        <p>
          The published data describes countries, organisations, models, legal instruments and
          aggregate populations. Individuals appear only where already named in a cited public
          record, such as the author of a paper or the publisher of a government document. No
          personal data about readers is held.
        </p>

        <h2>Rights</h2>
        <p>
          Australian privacy law and the GDPR confer rights over personal information. The
          analytics described above do not identify individuals, so no record held here relates to
          an identifiable reader. Requests concerning personal information may be made through the
          <a href="/corrections/">corrections page</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          A content blocker or browser tracking-protection setting will prevent the analytics
          script loading. The site functions identically without it.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>
          Changes to this policy are published here and the date above is updated. Changes
          affecting what is collected are also listed on the
          <a href="/corrections/">corrections page</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
